+/* Patch 2116 (RSX pass 110), ENHANCEMENT (display only): the render-rate fill. KZ3's first-person camera Rep shows
+ * the body at the FRAME's game time: Rep yaw = logic yaw - (1 - alpha) x the last look update's yaw delta (alpha =
+ * the Rep's slot fraction, Rep+0x124; measured on 7 K2 runs of RSX pass 107: the model matches the counts taken + pending
+ * within 1.3 ms sd at a 200 counts/s turn, the RE notes "Pass 110"). So the drawn view lags the counts by the
+ * consumed-but-not-shown part (1 - alpha) x take plus the counts not taken yet (the slot clock keeps them for the next
+ * update). The fill adds both: drawn = logic + pending = every count that arrived by the writer call, each count shown
+ * once (a take moves counts from "pending" to "logic"; alpha moves them from the (1 - alpha) term into the Rep). Patch
+ * 2112's latch added only the pending part, so its error was the alpha-dependent (1 - alpha) x take (worse than none on
+ * the slot clock, pass 107). take_dyaw/take_dpitch = the last update's applied deltas (0 when it took nothing);
+ * pend_* = pad_look_latch_delta for the peeked counts. alpha outside [0, 1] is clamped (NaN = 1: nothing consumed is
+ * added). */
+static inline void pad_look_fill_delta(float alpha, float take_dyaw, float take_dpitch, float pend_dyaw, float pend_dpitch,
+                                       float* dyaw, float* dpitch)
+{
+    if (!(alpha >= 0.0f)) alpha = alpha < 0.0f ? 0.0f : 1.0f;
+    if (alpha > 1.0f) alpha = 1.0f;
+    *dyaw = (1.0f - alpha) * take_dyaw + pend_dyaw;
+    *dpitch = (1.0f - alpha) * take_dpitch + pend_dpitch;
+}
